remstart
    THE BUBBLED FISH. a PROTOTYPE (Chris, 2026-10-27). the routines are in fish_routines_bubbled, and the
    tests in fish_tests_bubbled. a big group pushed out brings a rainbow fish (see fish_headers_rainbow),
    and a big group pushed in brings a bubble, so every big group is a choice of which one the player wants.

    WHERE IT COMES FROM. a group of BUBBLED_GROUP_SIZE fish or more, that matched, and pops, with the fish
    that the cursor is on IN it (the cursor carried a fish into the group, and finished it): that fish does
    not pop with the group. it is taken out of it, and a bubble closes around it (bubbledAhead). the group
    still counts it, for a bottle. one bubble for every such group, so there can be many on the board. no
    bubble is made on coral, though: that fish pops with its group.

    IT MOVES FOR FREE. a swap that moves a fish in a bubble, whichever end of the swap it is on, is not a
    move, for as long as the bubble lasts: there are no charges to use up (Chris, 2026-10-28). it is not
    counted, and the multiplier does not hear of it (bubbledSwapMade, from stepLiveMove in fish_funcs). but
    the board is looked at after it, the same as after any swap, so whatever it puts together pops: the
    fish that it moved out of the way, and the fish in the bubble too, which bursts with its group
    (Chris, 2026-10-28).

    HOW IT ENDS. a bubble lasts until one of these (Chris, 2026-10-28):
    - its fish is in a group that pops. the bubble bursts with it, and scores BUBBLED_POP_POINTS, with the
      multiplier.
    - it touches another bubble, side by side. the two come together, and both fish pop, as a group of
      their own, whatever kinds they are, and each bubble scores. so too many bubbles get in each other's
      way: a free swap has to keep them apart. they are found when handle_combos looks at the board
      (bubbledSettle), which it does after every swap: one swapped next to another, one made next to
      another, or one that falls next to another.
    - it lands on coral. the bubble bursts, and scores, and its fish is an ordinary fish again, where it
      is. it is looked at for that as soon as a swap puts it there, and on every look at the board, for one
      that fell there.

    THE BURST IS A MOMENT OF ITS OWN (Chris, 2026-10-28). when a look at the board finds bubbles whose fish
    are going to pop, they burst first, one after another, each with a pop, a big score of its own and a
    spray of bubbles, and every pop of that look waits for them (bubbledMomentAhead, from handle_combos,
    which puts it in ghostWait). then the look goes on, and the fish pop with their groups. the scores go
    in as the look is judged, but the words and the sounds wait for their time (BUBBLED_MOMENT_*, played by
    stepBubbled), because a score text that waits can show for a frame before its wait starts.

    HOW IT LOOKS. a cartoon bubble around the fish, the kind that floats out of a bubble wand: clear in the
    middle, one thin rim that wobbles and shimmers pink and blue, and a curved white shine (stepBubbled, and
    BubbledEffect.fx). the fish floats around inside it, and rocks, and is seen through it as through a
    ball of glass, bigger in the middle, and lit as if it were round (the fish loop of update_frame, and A
    FISH IN A BUBBLE in FishEffect.fx). the charges left are NOT shown: the player has to remember them
    (Chris, 2026-10-28). a little bubble floats off with every swap. a new bubble grows in with a boing: it
    overshoots, squashes and stretches, and its rim wobbles hard before it settles, while the fish starts to
    float. when it goes, used up or popped, it swells, its rim breaks up into pieces that fly off, and it
    fades (BUBBLED_BURST, which keeps going after the cell has forgotten the bubble). two that come
    together burst, with bubbles between them.

    STILL TO DO. a bubble is not saved with the game. a quest that counts moves sees a free swap the same
    way that it sees the swap of the "free move" card.
remend

global BUBBLED_ON = 1 `0 turns them off, for the debug window and the tests
global BUBBLED_GROUP_SIZE = 5 `how big a group the cursor has to push a fish into, for a bubble
global BUBBLED_POP_POINTS = 50 `what a bubble scores when it bursts, before the multiplier
global dim BUBBLED_AT(400) `1 when the fish in each cell is in a bubble. it goes with the fish.
global dim BUBBLED_PAID(400) `1 when the bubble of the fish in each cell has burst ahead of its pop, as a moment of its own, and scored. it goes with the fish.
global BUBBLED_MOMENT_MS = 520 `how long the pops of a look wait for the first bubble that bursts in it, in milliseconds
global BUBBLED_MOMENT_EVERY = 200 `and how long after it each of the others bursts
global BUBBLED_MOMENT_TEXT# = 1.5 `how big the words of a burst are, against the usual ones
#constant BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX 8
global dim BUBBLED_MOMENT_CELL(BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX) `the cell of each burst that is still to come, plus 1, or 0 for a free slot
global dim BUBBLED_MOMENT_AT(BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX) `when it bursts, in game ms
global dim BUBBLED_MOMENT_POINTS(BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX) `what it scored
global dim BUBBLED_MOMENT_NTH(BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX) `which burst of its look it is, from 0, so that each pops a little higher
global dim BUBBLED_SFX(BUBBLED_MOMENT_MAX)
global BUBBLED_SFX_LOADED = 0
global BUBBLED_VOL# = .9
global FORCE_BUBBLED = 7 `the forced group of the bubbles that came together. see FORCED POPS in fish_headers.
global BUBBLED_GROUP = -1 `the group of this look that a fish was taken out of, for a bubble, or -1
global BUBBLED_COUNT = 0 `how many bubbles have been made, for the tests
global BUBBLED_FREE_SWAPS = 0 `how many free swaps there have been, for the tests

` HOW IT LOOKS
#constant BUBBLED_SHOWN_MAX 8
global dim BUBBLED_SPRITE(BUBBLED_SHOWN_MAX) `the bubbles
global BUBBLED_SPRITES_MADE = 0
global BUBBLED_FX_ID
global BUBBLED_SIZE# = .95 `how big a bubble is, in cells, across
global BUBBLED_SPRITE_CELLS# = 1.1 `how big its sprite is, in cells, so that its rim has room to wobble
global BUBBLED_RIM# = 1 `how thick its rim is, in pixels of the screen
global BUBBLED_ALPHA = 235
global BUBBLED_WOBBLE# = .06 `how far the fish floats around inside, in its own size
global BUBBLED_WOBBLE_TURN# = .35 `and how far it rocks, in radians
global BUBBLED_WOBBLE_SPEED# = 1 `how fast it does
global BUBBLED_LENS# = .45 `how much bigger the middle of the bubble shows the fish
global BUBBLED_LENS_SHADE# = .45 `how much darker the fish is on the side of it away from the light
global BUBBLED_LENS_BLUE# = .8 `how much bluer it is close to the edge of the bubble
global dim BUBBLED_BORN_AT(400) `when the bubble of the fish in each cell was made, in game ms. it goes with the fish.
global BUBBLED_GROW_MS = 560 `how long a new bubble takes to grow in and settle
global BUBBLED_BURST_MS = 300 `how long a bubble takes to burst
#constant BUBBLED_BURST_MAX 8
global dim BUBBLED_BURST_SPRITE(BUBBLED_BURST_MAX)
global dim BUBBLED_BURST_X#(BUBBLED_BURST_MAX) `where each burst is
global dim BUBBLED_BURST_Y#(BUBBLED_BURST_MAX)
global dim BUBBLED_BURST_AT(BUBBLED_BURST_MAX) `when it bursts, in game ms. until then it is a whole bubble. 0 is a free slot.
global ORDER_BUBBLED = 21 `on top of the fish, and underneath the icons of the quests
